Error [E0121]: `evens` was consumed by `.to_list()`, so it can't be used here
  --> tests/ui/loop_move_reuse_next_iteration.jet:7:16
    |
  7 |         print(^evens.to_list())
    |                ^^^^^
  --> tests/ui/loop_move_reuse_next_iteration.jet:7:16
    |
  7 |         print(^evens.to_list())
    |                ^^^^^ `evens` moved to `.to_list()` here on an earlier loop iteration
 Why: After a value moves somewhere else, its old name no longer gives access to it
 Fix: Stop using `evens` after the move, or give `.to_list()` a copy with `evens.copy()` where it moved.
 Note: `evens` is one-pass — materialize it first with `evens.to_list()`, or create a fresh source for the second drive
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E0121
